The Mercedes-Benz C63 AMG Edition 507 is a high-performance variant of the W204 C63 AMG, produced for the 2014 and 2015 model years (Source [1, 4, 12, 26]). It was essentially an upgraded version of the standard C63 with the Development Package, featuring components from the SLS AMG engine and the Black Series hood (Source [1, 4, 6, 10, 11, 22, 24]). This evaluation is based on the Edition 507 relative to the current automotive market.

*   **price\_usd**: Original price was high, around $70,000 - $87,000 USD (Source [1, 11]). Current market values for well-maintained examples are still significant, ranging from $71,000 to $81,000+ (Source [26]). This is well above the market average for a new car. Score: -0.70.
*   **total\_cost\_estimate\_5yr\_usd**: High purchase price (as a used performance car), high maintenance, and potentially high repair costs contribute to a very high 5-year cost of ownership. Score: -0.90.
*   **insurance\_usd\_yr**: High-performance AMG models have very high insurance costs due to power, value, and repair expense. Score: -0.90.
*   **maint\_usd\_yr**: The naturally aspirated 6.2L V8 and performance components require specialized and expensive maintenance (Source [16]). Score: -0.90.
*   **repair\_risk\_score**: The M156 V8 is generally robust, especially the later versions with SLS internals like in the 507 (Source [16]). However, it's an older, high-performance engine with some known potential issues (camshaft adjusters mentioned as a possibility, though less common on later models) (Source [16]). Risk is higher than average but perhaps slightly better than the Black Series due to less extreme tuning. Score: -0.40.
*   **hp**: 507 hp (Source [1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15, 17, 19, 20, 21, 22, 24, 27, 30]). This is significantly above the average car today. Score: 0.90.
*   **torque**: 450 lb-ft (610 Nm) (Source [1, 3, 4, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15, 17, 20, 21, 22, 24, 30]). Also well above average. Score: 0.80.
*   **cylinder\_count**: V8 (8 cylinders) (Source [1, 3, 4, 7, 8, 10, 14, 15, 17, 20, 21]). Above the common 4 or 6 cylinders. Score: 0.50.
*   **engine\_displacement**: 6.2L (6208 cc) V8 (Source [1, 3, 4, 7, 8, 10, 14, 15, 17, 20, 21]). Very large displacement by modern standards. Score: 0.90.
*   **accel\_0\_60\_sec**: Around 3.6-4.2 seconds (Source [1, 3, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 19, 22, 27, 30]). Very fast acceleration, comparable to many modern performance cars. Score: 0.90.
*   **top\_speed**: Electronically limited to 174 mph (280 km/h) (Source [3, 4, 6, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 19, 22, 24, 30]). High top speed. Score: 0.60.
*   **drive\_type**: RWD (Source [1, 3, 6, 15, 23]). Score: 1.00 (based on guide).
*   **transmission\_type**: 7-speed AMG Speedshift MCT automatic (Source [1, 3, 4, 7, 10, 11, 14, 15, 21, 22, 24]). This is a multi-clutch automatic. The guide lists "Automatic Transmission" as +1.00. Sticking to the guide. Score: 1.00.
*   **offroad\_ability**: Designed purely for performance, low ground clearance (around 101-112mm or 4-4.4 inches) (Source [20, 26]), stiff suspension. Score: 1.00 (based on guide examples).
*   **braking\_dist\_ft**: Equipped with high-performance AMG composite brakes (Source [4, 6, 10, 11, 13, 22, 24, 27, 29]). Praised for stopping power (Source [6, 10, 24, 29]). Score: 0.50.
*   **size**: Length around 4581-4710mm (180-185 inches) (Source [7, 17, 20, 21, 26, 31]). Around the 4600mm average. Score: 0.00.
*   **wheelbase**: 2760-2765mm (108.7-108.9 inches) (Source [1, 15, 17, 20, 21, 26]). Around the 2700mm average. Score: 0.00.
*   **body\_style**: Available as Sedan, Coupe, and Estate (Source [3, 4, 10, 11, 24]). Score: 0.00.
*   **seats**: 4 seats (Coupe) or 5 seats (Sedan/Estate) (Source [1, 17, 20, 23, 26]). Score: 0.00.
*   **cargo\_space**: Sedan cargo volume around 12.4 cu ft (Source [12]). Coupe around 11.7 cu ft (Source [12]). Below the 15 cu ft average. Score: -0.50.
*   **rear\_space**: Limited rear space, especially in the Coupe. Score: -0.50.
*   **ground\_clearance\_in**: Around 101-112mm (4-4.4 inches) (Source [20, 26]). Very low due to performance focus. Score: -1.00.
*   **turn\_radius\_ft**: Around 10.80-10.84m (35.4-35.6 ft) (Source [15, 20, 21, 26]). Around the 36 ft average. Score: 0.00.
*   **mpg**: Very poor fuel economy, EPA combined around 15 mpg (Source [1, 6, 15, 18, 20, 26]). Real-world often lower (Source [1, 18]). Score: -1.00.
*   **co2\_g\_km**: High emissions due to large V8 and poor fuel economy. Around 280-285 g/km (Source [3]). Score: -1.00.
*   **electric\_range\_mi**: Not electric. Score: -1.00.
*   **charge\_speed\_kw**: Not applicable. Score: -1.00.
*   **style\_sleek\_vs\_boxy**: W204 C-Class shape is a classic sedan/coupe, neither particularly sleek nor boxy. Score: 0.00.
*   **style\_aggression\_rating**: Features the Black Series hood, unique wheels, and AMG styling (Source [1, 4, 6, 10, 11, 13, 22, 24]). Aggressive appearance. Score: 0.80.
*   **style\_modernity\_rating**: Design is from the early 2010s. Looks dated compared to current designs. Score: -0.60.
*   **handling\_rating**: Praised for engaging handling, steering feel, and ability to manage power (Source [2, 5, 6, 29, 32]). While perhaps not as ultimately fast through corners as some modern rivals (Source [2]), it's highly communicative (Source [2]). Score: 0.80.
*   **ride\_comfort\_rating**: Suspension is firm, especially with the sport tuning, but reviews suggest it's manageable, though harsh on poor surfaces (Source [5, 6, 29]). Score: -0.50.
*   **cabin\_noise\_rating**: The loud V8 exhaust is a key feature (Source [1, 2, 8, 19, 32]), but cabin insulation is decent for a performance car of its era. Score: -0.20.
*   **shift\_smooth\_rating**: MCT can be quick but sometimes clunky at low speeds (Source [2]). Score: -0.20.
*   **steering\_feel\_rating**: Hydraulic steering is often praised for its feel and communication (Source [2, 5, 6]). Score: 0.80.
*   **adas\_score**: Minimal ADAS features for its era. Score: -1.00.
*   **visibility\_rating**: Standard sedan/coupe visibility. Score: 0.00.
*   **headlight\_rating**: Bi-xenon headlights likely standard. Good for their time, but not modern adaptive LEDs. Score: -0.20.
*   **security\_rating**: Standard for a luxury performance car of its time. Score: 0.00.
*   **screen\_in**: Small screen by modern standards (7-inch COMAND) (Source [6]). Score: -0.80.
*   **infotainment\_ux\_rating**: Dated COMAND system (Source [6]). Score: -0.80.
*   **smartphone\_connect\_rating**: Basic connectivity (Bluetooth) (Source [23]). No modern smartphone integration. Score: -1.00.
*   **audio\_rating**: Optional Harman/Kardon system available (Source [13]). Good for its time, but not best-in-class today. Score: 0.00.
*   **usb\_ports**: Likely one or two ports. Score: -0.50.
*   **comfort\_feature\_score**: Heated seats, power seats, dual-zone climate available (Source [13]). Basic luxury features for its era. Score: -0.20.
*   **convenience\_feature\_score**: Rearview camera, parking sensors available (Source [13]). Lacks modern convenience tech. Score: -0.20.
*   **brand\_prestige\_rating**: Mercedes-Benz AMG. High prestige. Score: 0.90.
*   **model\_prestige\_rating**: C Class is mid-range, but C63 is a high-performance variant, and the Edition 507 is a special, more powerful version (Source [6, 10, 11, 13, 14, 19, 24]). Score: -0.50.
*   **trim\_prestige\_rating**: Edition 507 is a highly desirable, near-top-tier performance trim, just below the Black Series (Source [6, 10, 13]). Score: -0.90.
*   **interior\_luxury\_rating**: Alcantara, leather, sport seats, special badging (Source [6, 10, 11, 13, 24]). Based on an older C-Class interior, less luxurious than modern high-end interiors. Score: 0.40.
*   **interior\_tech\_focus\_rating**: Minimal tech focus compared to modern cars. Score: -0.80.

